  "about": "How an identity's keys come from its recovery phrase: BIP39 seed (PBKDF2-HMAC-SHA512, 2048 rounds, salt \"mnemonic\"), then SLIP-0010 Ed25519 with every step hardened. Key n of an identity is at m/44'/0'/0'/0'/n': 0 founds it, 1 is what founding commits to, n+1 is what the rotation to key n commits to. public_key_qb64 is the key in CESR with code D. Checked by identity-agent-core/backup and by the app's key manager.",
